# The Skill Manager reached the way a level-up reaches it, and one
# unrecognised key. This is the second half of the oracle for inc-0o0r.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/skill-manager-levelup.keys 5
#
# WHY THIS NEEDS NO EXPERIENCE POINTS. The character sheet's [S] calls
# MyTerm->SkillManager() with no argument (src/Managers.cpp:2318), and the
# default argument is false (inc/Term.h:731). That is the same call a level-up
# makes, and the same `initial == false` the defect's second half needs. The
# wizard 'Generate 50 XP Ticks' route would need 1000 XP for a Barbarian's
# second level -- twenty visits to the menu -- and would prove nothing extra.
#
# The two halves of inc-0o0r are one arm of one switch wearing two faces. With
# ranks still unspent, as in character generation, the arm ran Reset and threw
# the allocations away; with the pool empty, as here, it fell through to the
# return and shut the manager without a word. So the claim to test here is not
# "the ranks survive" -- there are none to place -- it is "the manager is still
# open".
#
# Menu letters are lowercase on purpose. StandardKeySet holds
# { KY_CMD_CHAR_SHEET, 'D', 0 } and matches toupper(ch) against that raw key
# with the modifier flags compared exactly (src/Tables.cpp:4736), so the key
# that opens the sheet is lowercase d and never shift-D. The sheet then reads
# its own menu through toupper() (src/Managers.cpp:2283), so lowercase s
# reaches its case 'S'.
#
# Four screen dumps. The comparison between them is the whole test:
#
#   open        the Skill Manager, opened from the character sheet.
#   after-end   after one END. It MUST still be the Skill Manager, and MUST
#               equal "open" -- END is not a key this screen knows.
#   after-home  after one HOME. Same requirement.
#   after-esc   after ESC answered 'y'. ESC is the one key that MAY close
#               this screen, and it MUST have asked first.
#
# Before the fix, "after-end" is the character sheet: the manager closed on a
# keystroke that means nothing to it. See tools/check_skill_manager_reset.sh.

@include chargen.keys

d                   # character sheet
s                   # [S] Skills -- SkillManager(false), the level-up path
@dump:open

END                 # left stick DOWN-LEFT
@dump:after-end
HOME                # left stick UP-LEFT
@dump:after-home

ESC y               # the one key that may leave, and it asks now
@dump:after-esc

ESC                 # leave the character sheet
@quit
